# Code of Conduct

## Our Commitment

This project is committed to providing a welcoming, respectful, and professional environment for everyone who interacts with the repository.

All participants are expected to contribute positively by promoting constructive discussions, knowledge sharing, and mutual respect.

---

# Expected Behaviour

Contributors are encouraged to:

- Be respectful and considerate in all interactions.
- Provide constructive feedback and suggestions.
- Maintain a professional and collaborative attitude.
- Respect different opinions and perspectives.
- Focus discussions on improving the project.

---

# Unacceptable Behaviour

The following behaviours are not acceptable:

- Harassment or discrimination of any kind.
- Offensive or inappropriate language.
- Personal attacks or disrespectful comments.
- Spam, misleading information, or promotional content unrelated to the project.
- Any behaviour that creates an unprofessional or hostile environment.

---

# Communication Guidelines

Please ensure that all communication:

- Remains respectful and professional.
- Is relevant to the project.
- Supports collaboration and continuous improvement.
- Encourages learning and knowledge sharing.

---

# Scope

This Code of Conduct applies to all interactions related to this repository, including:

- Issues
- Discussions
- Pull Requests
- Project documentation
- Any other project-related communication

---

# Enforcement

Project maintainers reserve the right to remove, edit, or reject comments, contributions, or interactions that violate this Code of Conduct.

Repeated or serious violations may result in restricted participation within the repository.

